---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const MANIFEST = '/releases';
const DOCS = 'https://docs.freesense.org';
---

<Base
  title="Download FreeSense"
  description="Download manifest-driven FreeSense installer images for amd64 and verify their provenance and SHA-256 checksums."
>
  <section class="download-hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Download center</span>
        <h1>Your firewall starts<br /><span>with a verifiable build.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Choose the supported Stable line or an experimental Development build, verify one
          checksum, and install or import on standard amd64 hardware. Every published image is tied to exact
          source, ports, OS-definition, and FreeBSD revisions.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#release-channels">View available images</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${DOCS}/getting-started/installation/`}>Installation guide</a>
        </div>
        <div class="platform-row" aria-label="Supported platform">
          <span>amd64</span><span>UEFI + BIOS</span><span>Signed repositories</span><span>Apache-2.0</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="release-terminal" aria-label="FreeSense release model">
        <div class="terminal-head"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>release contract</span></div>
        <div class="terminal-body mono">
          <p><b>$</b> resolve build-set</p>
          <p><em>source</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>ports</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>os-definition</em><span>exact commit</span></p>
          <p><em>freebsd</em><span>frozen snapshot</span></p>
          <div class="terminal-rule"></div>
          <p class="terminal-ok">verified artifacts only</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="release-channels" class="release-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Release channels</span>
          <h2>Pick the right level of change.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Stable 1.0.x is the supported production line. Development 1.1 is experimental, intended only for testing, and comes without support.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="channels" class="channels" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="loading"><span></span>Reading the release manifest...</div>
      </div>
      <p class="manifest-note">
        The website stores no release versions. It reads independently published{' '}
        <a href={`${MANIFEST}/stable.json`}>Stable</a>{' '}and{' '}
        <a href={`${MANIFEST}/devel.json`}>Development</a>{' '}documents live from the package service;
        installer and cloud-image links point to immutable files on the download service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pipeline-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Independent build flow</span><h2>Rebuild only what changed.</h2></div>
        <p>System updates and optional packages have separate fingerprints, repositories, and publication decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Check the System</h3><p>A daily planner builds and publishes the System repository only when its sealed inputs change.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Reuse optional packages</h3><p>Optional packages are reused while their sources and the pinned FreeBSD platform are unchanged. A System-only change does not rebuild them.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Publish after verification</h3><p>The ISO, QCOW2, and raw image must all pass integrity and boot-smoke checks. All immutable files are public before the channel document advances.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="architecture-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">What is inside</span>
      <h2>A smaller, sharper platform.</h2>
      <div class="architecture-grid">
        <article><strong>32</strong><h3>Curated packages</h3><p>Each package declares capabilities, services, support state, and resource impact before installation.</p></article>
        <article><strong>8</strong><h3>Suricata generation</h3><p>Validated atomic configuration, EVE event browsing, service controls, and a focused security overview.</p></article>
        <article><strong>2</strong><h3>Modern network additions</h3><p>First-class CrowdSec response and consent-driven ZeroTier networking, integrated into the WebUI.</p></article>
        <article><strong>1</strong><h3>Sealed build set</h3><p>Every stage consumes the same resolved commits. Channel metadata points to exact verified artifacts; publication never rebuilds them.</p></article>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${DOCS}/packages/installing-packages/`}>Explore the package platform <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Installation</span><h2>From image to gateway.</h2></div>
        <p>Use a dedicated appliance or VM with at least two interfaces, or one VLAN-capable interface.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="install-steps">
        <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Verify the download</h3><p>Compare the ISO with the published SHA-256 checksum.</p><code>sha256sum FreeSense-*.iso</code></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Write the installer</h3><p>Flash the ISO directly to a 4 GB or larger USB device with Rufus, Etcher, or dd.</p><code>dd if=FreeSense-*.iso of=/dev/DEVICE bs=4M conv=fsync</code></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Boot and configure</h3><p>Assign WAN and LAN, open the WebUI, then replace the initial administrator password.</p><a href={`${DOCS}/getting-started/first-boot/`}>First-boot guide</a></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="requirements"><b>Recommended starting point</b><span>64-bit CPU</span><span>4 GB RAM</span><span>16 GB storage</span><span>2 network interfaces</span></div>
      <p class="cloud-warning"><strong>Cloud networking:</strong> Use two NICs so management remains on LAN. A one-NIC image permits key-only WAN SSH only when metadata supplies a valid key; restrict it with a cloud security group. The WebUI is never opened on WAN automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script define:vars={{ MANIFEST }}>
  const channelMeta = {
    stable: { label: 'Stable', badge: 'Supported', description: 'Immutable 1.0.x releases for production deployments.', featured: true },
    devel: { label: 'Development', badge: 'Experimental', description: 'Rolling 1.1 builds for contributors, labs, and early testing.' },
  };

  const escapeHtml = (value) => String(value ?? '')
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  const size = (bytes) => {
    const value = Number(bytes);
    if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) return '';
    if (value >= 1024 ** 3) return `${(value / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(2)} GiB`;
    return `${Math.round(value / 1024 ** 2)} MiB`;
  };
  const shortSha = (value) => value ? String(value).slice(0, 12) : 'not recorded';
  const releaseDate = (value) => {
    if (!value) return '';
    const date = new Date(value);
    if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return '';
    return `${new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', {
      dateStyle: 'medium',
      timeStyle: 'short',
      timeZone: 'UTC',
    }).format(date)} UTC`;
  };
  const changeTypes = {
    security: 'Security',
    fix: 'Fix',
    feature: 'Feature',
    ui: 'Interface',
    package: 'Package',
    documentation: 'Docs',
    build: 'Build',
    other: 'Change',
  };

  function provenanceBlock(release) {
    const p = release.provenance;
    if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return '';
    return `<details class="channel-details"><summary>Build provenance</summary><dl>
      <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.source))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Ports</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.ports))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>OS definition</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.os_definition))}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>FreeBSD</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(shortSha(p.freebsd))}</dd></div>
    </dl></details>`;
  }

  function changesBlock(release) {
    const changes = Array.isArray(release.changes) ? release.changes.slice(0, 20) : [];
    if (!changes.length) {
      return `<details class="channel-details changes empty">
        <summary><span>What changed</span><small>Not published</small></summary>
        <p>Release notes are not available for this build yet.</p>
      </details>`;
    }
    const rows = changes.map((change) => {
      const type = Object.hasOwn(changeTypes, change.type) ? change.type : 'other';
      const scope = change.scope ? `<span>${escapeHtml(change.scope)}</span>` : '';
      return `<li><i class="change-type ${type}">${changeTypes[type]}</i><div>
        <strong>${escapeHtml(change.title)}</strong>${scope}
      </div></li>`;
    }).join('');
    return `<details class="channel-details changes">
      <summary><span>What changed</span><small>${changes.length} ${changes.length === 1 ? 'change' : 'changes'}</small></summary>
      <ol>${rows}</ol>
    </details>`;
  }

  function channelCard(key, release) {
    const meta = channelMeta[key];
    const notice = key === 'devel'
      ? '<div class="channel-notice experimental"><strong>Experimental &mdash; no support</strong><span>For labs and testing, never production.</span></div>'
      : '<div class="channel-notice supported"><strong>Recommended for production</strong><span>Immutable and supported throughout the 1.0.x line.</span></div>';
    const supported = key !== 'stable' || release?.support_tier === 'supported';
    const artifacts = release?.schema_version === 'freesense.download/v2'
      ? release.artifacts
      : release?.url ? [{
        kind: 'installer', format: 'iso', url: release.url, size: release.size,
        sha256: release.sha256,
      }] : [];
    if (!Array.isArray(artifacts) || artifacts.length === 0 || !supported) {
      return `<article class="channel-card unavailable">
        <div class="channel-title"><h3>${meta.label}</h3><span>${meta.badge}</span></div>
        <p>${meta.description}</p>${notice}<div class="not-available">No published artifact</div>
      </article>`;
    }
    const version = release.version ? `FreeSense ${release.version}` : 'Current build';
    const generation = key === 'devel' && Number.isInteger(release.generation)
      ? `<span class="generation">Generation ${release.generation}</span>`
      : '<span class="generation stable">Stable release</span>';
    const metadata = [
      releaseDate(release.published_at || release.date)
        ? `<span><b>Published</b>${escapeHtml(releaseDate(release.published_at || release.date))}</span>`
        : '',
    ].filter(Boolean).join('');
    const labels = { iso: 'Installer ISO', qcow2: 'QCOW2 cloud image', raw: 'Raw GPT cloud image' };
    const downloads = artifacts.map((artifact) => `
      <a class="btn ${artifact.format === 'iso' && meta.featured ? 'btn-primary' : 'btn-ghost'}"
        href="${escapeHtml(artifact.url)}">${labels[artifact.format] || artifact.format}
        <small>${escapeHtml(size(artifact.size))}</small></a>`).join('');
    const checksum = `<details class="channel-details checksum"><summary>SHA-256 checksums</summary>
      ${artifacts.map((artifact) => `<p><b>${escapeHtml(labels[artifact.format] || artifact.format)}</b><code>${escapeHtml(artifact.sha256)}</code></p>`).join('')}
    </details>`;
    return `<article class="channel-card ${meta.featured ? 'featured' : ''}">
      <div class="channel-title"><h3>${meta.label}</h3><span>${meta.badge}</span></div>
      <p>${meta.description}</p>
      ${notice}
      <div class="version">
        <small>Latest installer</small>
        <div class="version-line"><strong>${escapeHtml(version)}</strong>${generation}</div>
        <div class="release-meta">${metadata}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="artifact-downloads">${downloads}</div>
      <div class="release-details">${changesBlock(release)}${provenanceBlock(release)}${checksum}</div>
    </article>`;
  }

  async function loadChannels() {
    const target = document.getElementById('channels');
    const channels = Object.fromEntries(await Promise.all(['stable', 'devel'].map(async (key) => {
      try {
        const response = await fetch(`${MANIFEST}/${key}.json`, { cache: 'no-store' });
        if (response.status === 404) return [key, null];
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('release document unavailable');
        const release = await response.json();
        if (!['freesense.download/v1', 'freesense.download/v2'].includes(release.schema_version)
            || release.channel !== key) {
          throw new Error('release document invalid');
        }
        return [key, release];
      } catch {
        return [key, null];
      }
    })));
    target.innerHTML = ['stable', 'devel'].map((key) => channelCard(key, channels[key])).join('');
  }
  loadChannels();
</script>

<style>
  .download-hero { position: relative; padding: 112px 0 84px; overflow: hidden; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(320px, .65fr); gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  h1 { margin: 16px 0 0; font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 74px); letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  h1 span { color: var(--coral-hi); }
  .lede { max-width: 720px; color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px); margin: 24px 0 0; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 34px; }
  .platform-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .platform-row span { padding: 5px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 7px; color: var(--muted); font: 12px var(--mono); background: rgba(13,17,23,.55); }
  .release-terminal { border: 1px solid var(--border-2); border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.86); box-shadow: 0 35px 90px rgba(0,0,0,.35); overflow: hidden; transform: rotate(1deg); }
  .terminal-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 13px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--ink-2); }
  .terminal-head i { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--border-2); }
  .terminal-head i:first-child { background: var(--coral); }
  .terminal-head span { margin-left: auto; color: var(--muted-2); font: 11px var(--mono); }
  .terminal-body { padding: 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .terminal-body p { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin: 9px 0; }
  .terminal-body b { color: var(--coral-hi); }
  .terminal-body em { color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; }
  .terminal-body span { color: #d2d9e3; }
  .terminal-rule { height: 1px; background: var(--border); margin: 18px 0; }
  .terminal-body .terminal-ok { color: var(--good); justify-content: flex-start; }
  .terminal-ok::before { content: 'OK'; border: 1px solid rgba(62,207,142,.35); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; }

  .release-section { background: rgba(19,25,34,.82); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .section-heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 48px; margin-bottom: 38px; }
  .section-heading h2, .architecture-section h2 { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); }
  .section-heading > p { max-width: 470px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
  .channels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .loading { grid-column: 1/-1; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 270px; color: var(--muted); }
  .loading span { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--coral); box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px var(--coral-soft); animation: pulse 1.4s infinite; }
  @keyframes pulse { 50% { opacity: .45; transform: scale(.8); } }
  :global(.channel-card) { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--ink-3), rgba(19,25,34,.82)); }
  :global(.channel-card.featured) { border-color: rgba(234,79,45,.55); box-shadow: inset 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.04), 0 18px 45px rgba(0,0,0,.18); }
  :global(.channel-title) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; }
  :global(.channel-title h3) { margin: 0; font-size: 23px; }
  :global(.channel-title span) { color: var(--coral-hi); border: 1px solid rgba(234,79,45,.35); background: var(--coral-soft); padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; }
  :global(.channel-card > p) { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 10px 0 18px; }
  :global(.channel-notice) { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 2px; min-height: 62px; padding: 10px 13px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 9px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.34); font-size: 12px; }
  :global(.channel-notice strong) { color: var(--text); }
  :global(.channel-notice span) { color: var(--muted); }
  :global(.channel-notice.experimental) { border-color: rgba(234,79,45,.35); background: var(--coral-soft); }
  :global(.channel-notice.experimental strong) { color: var(--coral-hi); }
  :global(.channel-notice.supported) { border-color: rgba(62,207,142,.24); background: rgba(62,207,142,.055); }
  :global(.channel-notice.supported strong) { color: var(--good); }
  :global(.version) { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; margin-top: 16px; padding: 15px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.42); }
  :global(.version small) { color: var(--muted-2); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  :global(.version-line) { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px 14px; }
  :global(.version strong) { font: 600 18px var(--mono); word-break: break-word; }
  :global(.version .generation) { flex: 0 0 auto; color: var(--coral-hi); border: 1px solid rgba(234,79,45,.3); border-radius: 999px; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--coral-soft); font: 600 10px var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  :global(.version .generation.stable) { color: var(--good); border-color: rgba(62,207,142,.24); background: rgba(62,207,142,.055); }
  :global(.release-meta) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  :global(.release-meta span) { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
  :global(.release-meta b) { color: var(--muted-2); font-weight: 500; }
  :global(.channel-card .btn) { justify-content: center; margin: 14px 0 10px; text-align: center; }
  :global(.artifact-downloads) { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin: 10px 0; }
  :global(.artifact-downloads .btn) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin: 0; }
  :global(.artifact-downloads small) { opacity: .72; }
  :global(.checksum p) { margin: 10px 0; }
  :global(.checksum b) { display: block; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  :global(.not-available) { margin-top: auto; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 18px; color: var(--muted-2); font: 13px var(--mono); }
  :global(.release-details) { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  :global(.channel-details) { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  :global(.channel-details summary) { cursor: pointer; list-style-position: inside; }
  :global(.channel-details summary::marker) { color: var(--muted-2); }
  :global(.channel-details summary small) { float: right; color: var(--muted-2); font-size: 11px; }
  :global(.channel-details dl) { margin: 10px 0 0; }
  :global(.channel-details dl div) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; }
  :global(.channel-details dd) { margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--text); }
  :global(.checksum code) { display: block; margin-top: 8px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  :global(.changes > p) { margin: 10px 0 2px; color: var(--muted-2); }
  :global(.changes ol) { display: grid; gap: 1px; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 10px 0 2px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--border); }
  :global(.changes li) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 74px 1fr; gap: 10px; align-items: start; padding: 9px 10px; background: rgba(13,17,23,.82); }
  :global(.changes li div) { min-width: 0; }
  :global(.changes li strong) { display: block; color: var(--text); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4; }
  :global(.changes li div > span) { display: block; margin-top: 2px; color: var(--muted-2); }
  :global(.change-type) { width: fit-content; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(127,139,155,.12); color: var(--muted); font: 600 9px var(--mono); font-style: normal; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  :global(.change-type.security), :global(.change-type.fix) { color: var(--coral-hi); background: var(--coral-soft); }
  :global(.change-type.feature), :global(.change-type.ui) { color: var(--good); background: rgba(62,207,142,.07); }
  .manifest-note { text-align: center; color: var(--muted-2); font-size: 13px; margin: 24px 0 0; }

  .pipeline-section { padding-block: 90px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .pipeline-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 18px; }
  .pipeline-grid article { padding: 26px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--ink-2); }
  .pipeline-grid article > span { color: var(--coral-hi); font: 600 13px var(--mono); }
  .pipeline-grid h3 { margin: 14px 0 8px; font-size: 19px; }
  .pipeline-grid p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0; }

  .architecture-section { padding-block: 90px; }
  .architecture-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--border); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; margin: 36px 0 24px; }
  .architecture-grid article { padding: 28px; background: var(--ink-2); }
  .architecture-grid strong { font: 600 34px var(--mono); color: var(--coral-hi); }
  .architecture-grid h3 { margin: 13px 0 8px; font-size: 17px; }
  .architecture-grid p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0; }
  .text-link { font-weight: 600; }

  .install-section { background: var(--ink-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .section-heading.compact { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .install-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .install-steps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 75px 1fr; gap: 18px; padding: 28px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .install-steps li > span { color: var(--coral-hi); font: 600 14px var(--mono); }
  .install-steps h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 19px; }
  .install-steps p { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .requirements { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 24px; margin-top: 28px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .requirements b { color: var(--text); }
  .cloud-warning { margin: 18px 0 0; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid rgba(234,79,45,.35); border-radius: 9px; background: var(--coral-soft); color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .cloud-warning strong { color: var(--coral-hi); }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 42px; }
    .release-terminal { max-width: 560px; transform: none; }
    .channels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pipeline-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .architecture-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .download-hero { padding-top: 76px; }
    .section-heading { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
    .architecture-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .install-steps li { grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr; }
  }
</style>
